166 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 108 0 R
/T (Existing research identifies communication overhead as a major challenge in Federated Learning. FedAvg is a widely used baseline algorithm, while techniques such as model compression, gradient quantization, and adaptive client selection can reduce communication costs but may affect prediction accuracy. RFC 9000 defines QUIC, a secure transport protocol supporting multiplexed communication and low-latency connections. However, balancing communication efficiency, prediction accuracy, and real-time performance remains a key challenge in intelligent transportation systems. This project aims to evaluate these trade-offs and identify an efficient, scalable approach for real-time traffic prediction.)
/E (Existing research identifies communication overhead as a major challenge in Federated Learning. FedAvg is a widely used baseline algorithm, while techniques such as model compression, gradient quantization, and adaptive client selection can reduce communication costs but may affect prediction accuracy. RFC 9000 defines QUIC, a secure transport protocol supporting multiplexed communication and low-latency connections. However, balancing communication efficiency, prediction accuracy, and real-time performance remains a key challenge in intelligent transportation systems. This project aims to evaluate these trade-offs and identify an efficient, scalable approach for real-time traffic prediction.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
