180 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 109 0 R
/T (We propose a lightweight, decentralized framework for privacy-preserving traffic prediction with reduced communication overhead. Spatial-temporal models, such as ST-GCN or LSTM, will process traffic data locally at edge nodes, avoiding the need to transmit raw data to a central server. To reduce communication costs during federated aggregation, the framework will use adaptive gradient sparsification, model compression, and event-triggered updates based on significant traffic changes. The system will evaluate prediction accuracy, communication bandwidth, and transmission latency to identify an efficient balance between model performance and network resource consumption. This approach aims to support scalable, privacy-aware traffic forecasting for intelligent transportation systems.)
/E (We propose a lightweight, decentralized framework for privacy-preserving traffic prediction with reduced communication overhead. Spatial-temporal models, such as ST-GCN or LSTM, will process traffic data locally at edge nodes, avoiding the need to transmit raw data to a central server. To reduce communication costs during federated aggregation, the framework will use adaptive gradient sparsification, model compression, and event-triggered updates based on significant traffic changes. The system will evaluate prediction accuracy, communication bandwidth, and transmission latency to identify an efficient balance between model performance and network resource consumption. This approach aims to support scalable, privacy-aware traffic forecasting for intelligent transportation systems.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
