>>
endobj
714 0 obj
<<
/Title (Existing research identifies communication overhead as a major challenge in Federated Learning. FedAvg is a widely used baseline algorithm, while techniques such as model compression, gradient quantization, and adaptive client selection can reduce communication costs but may affect prediction accuracy. RFC 9000 defines QUIC, a secure transport protocol supporting multiplexed communication and low-latency connections. However, balancing communication efficiency, prediction accuracy, and real-time performance remains a key challenge in intelligent transportation systems. This project aims to evaluate these trade-offs and identify an efficient, scalable approach for real-time traffic prediction.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 636 0 R
/First 782 0 R
/Last 782 0 R
/Count -1
>>
endobj
